        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.117,
            0.845,
            0.157
          ],
          "content": "？ Find how many numbers lie between two consecutive perfect squares. Do you notice a pattern?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.161,
            0.847,
            0.234
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** If p & q are successive perfect square numbers, then there will be (q − p − 1) numbers between them. Yes."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.254,
            0.276,
            0.275
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Page No. 10"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.294,
            0.293,
            0.317
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.325,
            0.781,
            0.4
          ],
          "content": "1. Which of the following numbers are not perfect squares? (i) 2032 (ii) 2048 (iii) 1027 (iv) 1089 **Ans.** (i), (ii) and (iii)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.407,
            0.693,
            0.455
          ],
          "content": "2. Which one among 64<sup>2</sup>, 108<sup>2</sup>, 292<sup>2</sup>, 36<sup>2</sup> has last digit 4? **Ans.** 108<sup>2</sup> and 292<sup>2</sup>"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.462,
            0.621,
            0.533
          ],
          "content": "3. Given 125<sup>2</sup> = 15625, what is the value of 126<sup>2</sup>? (i) 15625 + 126 (ii) 15625 + 26<sup>2</sup> (iv) 15625 + 251 (v) 15625 + 51<sup>2</sup>"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.642,
            0.487,
            0.8,
            0.508
          ],
          "content": "(iii) 15625 + 253"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.538,
            0.242,
            0.557
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Ans. (iv)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.567,
            0.754,
            0.614
          ],
          "content": "4. Find the length of the side of a square whose area is 441 m<sup>2</sup>. **Ans.** 21 m"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.622,
            0.846,
            0.661
          ],
          "content": "5. Find the smallest square number that is divisible by each of the following numbers: 4, 9, and 10"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.667,
            0.246,
            0.686
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** 900"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.695,
            0.846,
            0.736
          ],
          "content": "6. Find the smallest number by which 9408 must be multiplied so that the product is a perfect square. Find the square root of the product."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.741,
            0.267,
            0.761
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** 3; 168"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.77,
            0.846,
            0.902
          ],
          "content": "7. How many numbers lie between the squares of the following numbers? (i) 16 and 17 **Ans.** 32 (ii) 99 and 100 **Ans.** 198"
        },
        {
